course: dictionary
lesson: 5020
title: Inform and information
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Inform is a doing word. It means to tell someone facts or news, especially in an official way. «Please inform a teacher if you feel unwell.» The teacher needs the facts so they can help you.
explain: «We are pleased to inform you that the trip is on.» Here inform is used in a letter, a polite and formal way of giving news. Letters and notices often use it.
explain: Inform also has a special meaning, inform on someone. It means to tell the police or a person in charge about something wrong someone did. Phrases like «keep someone informed» and «well informed» use the same root word.
explain: Add -tion and inform becomes information, a thing word. The -tion ending is a helpful clue: educate becomes education, and inform becomes information.
fact: Inform is a verb: inform, informs, informed, informing.
fact: «Inform» means to tell someone facts or news, especially officially.
fact: «Inform on someone» means to tell the police or a person in charge about something wrong someone did.
fact: «Keep someone informed» means keep them up to date with news.
fact: Adding -tion turns inform into information, a thing word.
exercise: «Please inform a teacher if you feel unwell.» What does inform mean here? | Hide from the teacher | *Tell a teacher the facts | Draw a picture for the teacher | Ask the teacher to sing
exercise: Adding -tion turns the verb inform into a thing word. Which word is it? | informed | *information | informing | informs
exercise: «We are pleased to inform you that the trip is on.» Where would you most likely read this sentence? | In a song about rain | On a sandwich wrapper | *In a letter giving official news | In a joke book
test: «Keep me informed about the match.» What does keep me informed mean? | Keep me away from the match | Keep me from talking | Keep me in a box | *Keep me up to date with news
test: Which meaning fits «well informed»? | Bored of school | Very hungry | *Knowing a lot about a subject | Mixed up about the facts
exam: Priya saw a classmate break the window and chose to inform on him. What does inform on mean here? | *Tell the person in charge about what he did | Forget about it and say nothing ever | Give him a present for being brave | Ask him to come and play
